{"id": "EUVD-2026-96712", "enisaUuid": "5ea3d8cf-b084-36da-80f0-f6ea801e0913", "description": "Wukong AICRM through 20260610 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated users to write into other users' AI chat sessions by supplying an arbitrary sessionId to POST /chat/send. Attackers can append messages to a victim's conversation and receive streamed assistant replies built from the victim's last 20 messages, disclosing conversation content.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T01:12:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:07", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/Wukong-AICRM/poc_chat_send.py", "https://github.com/WuKongOpenSource/Wukong-AICRM/blob/cdd1fbc3187d2bcbf2cdf2be7d50c988959da356/backend/src/main/java/com/kakarote/ai_crm/service/impl/ChatServiceImpl.java#L270-L283", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wukong-aicrm-through-20260610-authorization-bypass-via-user-controlled-session-id-in-post-chat-send"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108689", "GHSA-2p74-f492-56xr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "af0faef9-9a2c-3398-b74e-70ae87e0a734", "product": {"name": "Wukong AICRM", "vendor": {"name": "WuKongOpenSource"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260610"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "daf45985-daa4-3845-9a3f-0318a55ca9b4", "vendor": {"name": "WuKongOpenSource"}}], "isExploited": false}